WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.290
Say you're building a writing app.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.990
Writers keep private drafts,

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.800
and publish finished stories to a public feed.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.550
Your team writes its architecture down in

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.790
a Shape model file in the repo.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:12.860
One rule in it says

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.290
private drafts are never exported.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.520
You ask your coding agent for one small feature:

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.560
a share button.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.000
Seconds later, it's done.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.640
But it also shares private drafts.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.780
The model file also marks the

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.760
share code's folder as governed:

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.610
any change there must update the model file too,

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.230
or say why it doesn't need to.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.700
The agent's change didn't,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.870
so the Shape check on the pull request fails.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.940
So the agent adds what the

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.870
button does to the model file:

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.860
it exports a private draft.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.630
That breaks the team's rule,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.620
and a grant can't override it.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.560
The merge stops.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.640
Here the answer is obviously no.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.030
The agent fixes the code

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.940
to share only published stories,

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.200
and updates the model file to match.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:55.880
The check passes.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.160
If you did want drafts shared,

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.640
say with an editor,

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.760
you'd change the rule in the

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.600
model file along with the code,

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.840
and the pull request's review

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.090
would check that they match.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.480
Shape: architecture you can check in CI.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.550
Install shp, and start with one rule.
